From: SMS Backup+ modernization (story U-003)
Subject: [PATCH] GooglePlayDriver: add FLAG_IMMUTABLE to identity-token PendingIntent

Android 12 (API 31)+ throws IllegalArgumentException when a PendingIntent is created
without FLAG_IMMUTABLE or FLAG_MUTABLE. GooglePlayDriver's constructor created its
identity token without a flag, crashing any app that targets SDK 31+ at the point
BackupJobs is constructed (App.onCreate). The token is never mutated, so FLAG_IMMUTABLE
is correct. Guarded by SDK_INT >= 31 using the integer literal because this library
compiles against compileSdk 29, where Build.VERSION_CODES.S is not a named constant.

This patch is temporary: firebase-jobdispatcher is removed entirely by the WorkManager
migration (MU-005 / stories U-014, U-017).

--- a/jobdispatcher/src/main/java/com/firebase/jobdispatcher/GooglePlayDriver.java
+++ b/jobdispatcher/src/main/java/com/firebase/jobdispatcher/GooglePlayDriver.java
@@ -19,6 +19,7 @@ package com.firebase.jobdispatcher;
 import android.app.PendingIntent;
 import android.content.ComponentName;
 import android.content.Context;
 import android.content.Intent;
+import android.os.Build;
 import android.support.annotation.NonNull;
 import com.firebase.jobdispatcher.FirebaseJobDispatcher.ScheduleResult;

@@ -69,7 +70,15 @@ public final class GooglePlayDriver implements Driver {
   /** Instantiates a new GooglePlayDriver. */
   public GooglePlayDriver(@NonNull Context context) {
     this.context = context;
-    token = PendingIntent.getBroadcast(context, 0, new Intent(), 0);
+    // SMS Backup+ U-003 patch: Android 12 (API 31)+ requires an explicit mutability
+    // flag on PendingIntent or it throws IllegalArgumentException. This identity token
+    // is never mutated, so FLAG_IMMUTABLE is correct. (This library is removed by the
+    // WorkManager migration; this keeps the app launchable at targetSdk 31+ until then.)
+    // Build.VERSION_CODES.S (31) is not a named constant under this library's
+    // compileSdk 29, so the integer literal 31 is used. FLAG_IMMUTABLE = 0x4000000
+    // existed since API 23, so referencing it at compile time is safe.
+    int tokenFlags = (Build.VERSION.SDK_INT >= 31)
+        ? PendingIntent.FLAG_IMMUTABLE
+        : 0;
+    token = PendingIntent.getBroadcast(context, 0, new Intent(), tokenFlags);
     writer = new GooglePlayJobWriter();
     validator = new DefaultJobValidator(context);
   }
